<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to March 17 due to a rise in bank note circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   450.20 (+  1.77)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  14.07 (-  1.15)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.67 (unchanged)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.82 (+  1.98)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  96.68 (+  2.06)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   455.77 (+  3.21)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
